From 38a49872335f5d9c785065431078b208a8739028 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:32:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(camera): update JN1 read-only horizontal blanking
 metadata

Register HBLANK without hardware control operations. Its fixed value
comes from the selected sensor mode and has no writable register path.

While runtime PM keeps the sensor active, changing the range used to
call s5kjn1_set_ctrl and hit its unsupported-control error. V4L2 had
already changed the range but retained the previous current value,
causing frame-rate calculations to use the old line length. The NULL
operations let V4L2 commit this mode metadata independently of power
state while preserving the control's read-only userspace flag.
---
 drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c b/drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c
index d77aed92c78..a4255fbd933 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c
@@ -842,7 +842,7 @@ static int s5kjn1_init_controls(struct s5kjn1 *s5kjn1)
 					       0, pixel_rate, 1, pixel_rate);
 
 	hblank = mode->hts - mode->width;
-	s5kjn1->hblank = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(ctrl_hdlr, &s5kjn1_ctrl_ops,
+	s5kjn1->hblank = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(ctrl_hdlr, NULL,
 					   V4L2_CID_HBLANK, hblank,
 					   hblank, 1, hblank);
 	if (s5kjn1->hblank)
